WEBVTT

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.420
Echo 1 to all units! The enemy has breached defensive perimeter 2!

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:32.060
Echo 2, above you!

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:37.560
Echo 2!

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.360
The demon of Arandas?

00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:00.040
Command to all units. Mission complete.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:03.270
Repeat. Mission complete.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:13.890
Someday, in this space deprived of hope,
kono takaki mubou no kuu de itsuka

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:18.560
you'll kneel of your own will.
sono ishi wa hiza wo tateru

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:29.780
break up foreordination

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:34.660
Was that flame an illusion or a friend?
fake ano hi wa nakama ka

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:39.370
Am I to venture into the darkness?
susumu beki wa yami ka

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:48.670
You'll find nameless emotions beyond the protruding knife.
knife tsukitateta saki ni shoutai no mienu kanjou

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:54.510
I can't let this end here yet.
ima wa mada koko de owarenai

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:59.640
I need to get ready to survive.
naraba ikiru junbi wo shiro yo

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:04.940
The passion in my heart only burns hotter.
uzu takaku tsumiageteku netsujou

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:08.440
Needless to say, it burdens me.
omotai ni kimatten darou

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:09.900
wake up your tough intention

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:10.860
Go ahead and mock my inexperience on the battlefield.
mijuku da to warau ga ii sa senjou

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:15.120
mijuku da to warau ga ii sa senjou
Go ahead and mock my inexperience on the battlefield.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:21.750
I'll show you what I've got, bit by bit,
hitotsu zutsu tashikamete yaru kara

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:23.290
so bring it on.
kakattekoi

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:33.800
break up foreordination

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:40.020
Beloved citizens of Ingelmia.

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:43.170
Promise
Beloved citizens of Ingelmia.

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:44.940
Victory is right before our eyes!
Promise

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:45.860
Victory is right before our eyes!

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:50.860
It is plain as day that the cowardly, conniving, corrupt leaders of Arandas

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:56.410
no longer have the ability to lead their nation.

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:02.920
Let us liberate our friends in Arandas in the name of justice and freedom!

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:09.380
The people of that land are eagerly awaiting our arrival!

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:13.180
Please help me in this effort!

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:18.640
Let's all buy war bonds to help in the righteous battle to save Arandas.

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:23.510
The bond you buy will become a bullet that helps support our soldiers.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:26.130
Bonds can also be purchased via cell phone.

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:39.790
Yo.

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:46.370
It's been three years, huh?

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:47.870
You've aged.

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:49.610
I don't want to hear that from you.

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:50.770
Do I look older?

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:53.320
Yeah. I can see it on your face.

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:56.290
I see. I've gotta be more careful.

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:04.030
You still piloting a Trail Krieger?

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:05.980
It's kind of my thing.

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:14.020
I guess the rumors about you turning down every opportunity for promotion are true.

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:19.330
But you can't keep that up forever.

00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:21.340
Are you okay with that?

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:22.620
I'm fine.

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:25.480
I don't want to bear any burdens I don't have to.

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:27.530
You know that.

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:38.740
Since you won't ask, I'll tell you.

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:40.590
I'm a major now.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:44.300
Congratulations on your promotion, Major Conrad Daniels.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.990
Thanks, Second Lieutenant.

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:47.390
I guess it's true.

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:50.270
I know a guy in the 6th Battalion who says he saw it.

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:52.490
The demon of Arandas?

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:55.740
I heard it's a Trail Krieger with incredible specs.

00:04:55.740 --> 00:05:00.870
If Arandas would just surrender, we wouldn't have to fight.

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:04.290
I hope I don't have to see it before this thing's over.

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:10.290
It's true that soldiers value their lives more when victory is at hand,

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:13.350
and their blades become blunt.

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:15.640
The demon of Arandas?

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:18.380
It's called Argevollen or something.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:19.890
Argevollen?

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:22.920
The name of Arandas's new model.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:26.290
It's an old word that dates from before the axis inversion.

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:33.420
What was it like?

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:35.690
You know?

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:40.200
Yeah. I was worried you might be down.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:42.410
Mind your own business.

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:46.550
Well, either way, you should rest a little.

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:48.570
A change of pace now and then is important.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:50.170
I'll take you up on that.

00:05:57.270 --> 00:06:00.230
How'd you know I was here, Second Lieutenant Roderick?

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:03.430
That's top secret classified information.

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:06.970
I'm surprised.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:12.050
There aren't many people who can make him laugh the first time they see him.

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:14.690
It's your fault, Major.

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:18.380
This is Second Lieutenant Roderick, one of my subordinates.

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:20.200
Second Lieutenant Liz Roderick.

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:23.380
Schlein Richthofen.

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:26.160
I'm in plain clothes, so I'll pass on the salute.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:27.820
I know you.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:31.160
I've heard rumors about you from Major Daniels.

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:31.960
Rumors?

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:34.880
Like the apple cider incident at the academy...

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:36.730
Daniels...

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:39.880
Don't worry. I didn't tell her about the waitress.

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:41.180
Conrad!

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:42.990
Waitress?

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:45.140
Always save your best card for last.

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:48.470
I'll take a new bottle.

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:53.480
I'm heading to Zong.

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:56.470
We can have this to celebrate when we come back.

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:57.540
Zong?

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:00.460
You've got the order, too.

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:03.450
We're gathering our forces at the Zong base

00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:07.620
so we can blow open a hole in the Arandas defenses.

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:10.000
I'm in charge of security there.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.620
I see.

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:15.080
Okay, Schlein.

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:16.290
I'll see you there.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:17.920
Yeah.

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:32.400
Splendid.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:36.270
The shooting? Or the gun?

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:39.320
Both, I'd say.

00:07:42.010 --> 00:07:43.590
That second lieutenant...

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:45.290
What was his name again?

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:46.750
Richthofen?

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:48.210
Yes, him.

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:50.540
I'm impressed he made it back alive.

00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:52.020
Splendid.

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:52.730
Yes.

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:58.460
That new model was developed by an Arandas corporation named Kybernes.

00:07:58.460 --> 00:08:02.580
There's no need for Intelligence to hide that.

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:05.160
That's what interests me.

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:08.030
I don't know what Intelligence is thinking.

00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:13.560
But if it threatens His Excellency Junios's rule...

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:17.310
Bad weeds must be plucked early.

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:25.700
I'm happy from the bottom of my heart you and I share the same values, Colonel Holmes.

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:33.480
How was he?

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:35.470
A relic of a past era.

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:39.220
He believes he can control the whole war himself.

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:41.090
Is it okay to leave him alone?

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:46.520
In the end, he's just a braggart.

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:54.080
We'll just have him believe I'm his loyal servant for now.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:58.230
What can he accomplish with his musty old authoritarianism?

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:01.900
And our goal...

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:03.490
Yes.

00:09:05.780 --> 00:09:07.450
<b>Viltriveld</b>

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:10.360
The border struggle between East Laboria and the Orisis democracy
<b>Viltriveld</b>

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:11.740
has increased our profits by 12 percent.
<b>Viltriveld</b>

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:14.140
has increased our profits by 12 percent.

00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:17.550
Wasn't it supposed to be 15 percent?

00:09:17.550 --> 00:09:21.650
The Laborian forces are advancing faster than our original estimates.

00:09:21.650 --> 00:09:26.400
We're trying to convince their generals to slow the advance.

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:30.390
Why don't we supply more equipment to Orisis instead?

00:09:30.390 --> 00:09:34.680
There are a hundred lots of anti-tank missiles near their expiry dates

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:37.010
that are about to discarded at the northern maintenance depot.

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:38.400
An excellent idea.

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:40.890
We can sell those to Orisis, then.

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:44.900
What's going on with Arandas and Ingelmia?

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:48.740
Arandas was holding out well at the beginning,

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:54.030
but Ingelmia's persistent attacks are putting it in a bad position strategically.

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:57.420
How is Argevollen affecting the battle?

00:09:57.420 --> 00:10:01.320
A single Trail Krieger can't affect the entire war.

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:03.070
There should be no problem.

00:10:03.070 --> 00:10:04.760
I see.

00:10:05.390 --> 00:10:08.170
By the way, what happened with the pilot?

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:10.230
There's no problem with that.

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:14.920
There was an accident, so now there's a different pilot than originally planned,

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:17.840
but it's actually turned out better.

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:20.690
We may be able to move to the next phase sooner than expected.

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:23.610
We should thank the Brigadier General.

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:29.780
Thirty-six hours ago, a recon squad found an Ingelmia forward base.

00:10:29.780 --> 00:10:32.610
From the look of the base, Command determined

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:37.410
that it was intended to be used for a large-scale invasion of our nation.

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:39.710
We will strike this base.

00:10:39.710 --> 00:10:42.290
This is a preemptive attack mission.

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:45.210
We will be attacking in conjunction

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:48.690
with Karlfas's 6th Mobile Battalion and the 21st Artillery Battalion.

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:51.550
As for who's going...

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:53.050
Sergeant Appleton.

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:54.550
Corporal Juliano.

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:56.300
Private Susumu.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:59.120
Your Trail Krieger squad is to enter the base

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:01.190
and be the ones to ultimately capture it.

00:11:01.190 --> 00:11:05.850
It's believed that Ingelmia will begin its attack in 48 hours.

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:09.490
This is a precursor to a large-scale invasion.

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:14.470
But this also means that by destroying this base,

00:11:14.470 --> 00:11:18.080
we can blunt the enemy's assault.

00:11:18.710 --> 00:11:21.890
Independent Unit 8 will begin to move out now.

00:11:23.980 --> 00:11:25.710
Our target is Zong.

00:11:27.150 --> 00:11:28.770
Good luck.

00:11:33.470 --> 00:11:34.490
Okay!

00:11:34.490 --> 00:11:37.220
Relax a bit, Tokimune-kun.

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:40.770
I'm all right. Leave it to me.

00:11:40.770 --> 00:11:43.130
Oh, my. How encouraging.

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:44.560
Don't get cocky.

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:46.690
Yes, ma'am!

00:12:10.010 --> 00:12:11.260
We're going.

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:14.050
Yes, sir!

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:40.080
Come in.

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:42.290
Excuse me.

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:49.620
Commander Lintz, the 3rd mobile corps is going on standby.

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:53.690
The 4th and 5th corps will
begin resupply at 0900,

00:12:53.690 --> 00:12:56.470
and go on standby at 1300.

00:12:56.470 --> 00:12:58.070
Excellent.

00:12:58.070 --> 00:13:00.490
Sounds like everything's going as planned, Major.

00:13:00.490 --> 00:13:01.760
Yes, sir.

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:07.400
Once we begin our attack, Arandas will have no choice but to move its forces.

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:09.910
That will cause their defensive lines to collapse.

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:14.130
When that happens, Major, you'll be on the front lines.

00:13:14.130 --> 00:13:15.240
I'm counting on you.

00:13:15.240 --> 00:13:17.410
It's an honor, Colonel.

00:13:17.410 --> 00:13:22.160
I'll be the first person to plant our flag in Arandas's capital.

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:23.620
Major.

00:13:28.390 --> 00:13:30.090
What is it?

00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:32.130
That's a bad habit of yours, Major.

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:32.880
It is?

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:35.130
It's all about morale.

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:56.500
I'd like the troops to be a little more on the ball.

00:13:56.500 --> 00:14:00.480
Then, shall we hold a surprise equipment inspection in 20 minutes?

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:02.110
Yeah. Do that.

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:25.860
That's right.

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:29.120
As soon as you find out where they are, tell the artillery to hit them back!

00:14:29.120 --> 00:14:30.890
Mobilize all our Trail Kriegers!

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:32.650
Have them split up to—

00:14:38.150 --> 00:14:39.900
Major, the commander!

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:56.650
I'll take command. Give me a communicator.

00:14:56.650 --> 00:14:57.510
Yes, sir.

00:14:58.430 --> 00:15:01.500
Graveyard to all patrol squads.

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:04.300
This is Major Conrad Daniels.

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:08.560
Any patrol squads hearing this message, come in immediately!

00:15:08.560 --> 00:15:11.290
Graveyard to all patrol squads!

00:15:11.290 --> 00:15:14.220
We have engaged the enemy!

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:17.240
All patrol squads, respond immediately!

00:15:17.240 --> 00:15:19.320
This is your commander, Daniels—

00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:21.610
Why did you destroy it?

00:15:21.610 --> 00:15:23.820
We could've used it.

00:15:23.820 --> 00:15:26.460
They should have a code.

00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:29.330
And they'll be changing channels soon, too.

00:15:32.580 --> 00:15:36.020
Change all comm channels to Charlie 202.

00:15:36.020 --> 00:15:38.190
There's a chance the enemy is listening in.

00:15:38.190 --> 00:15:39.210
Yes, sir.

00:15:39.210 --> 00:15:40.430
Tell all forces.

00:15:40.430 --> 00:15:43.430
Roger. Changing channel to Charlie 202.

00:15:43.430 --> 00:15:45.680
The enemy's main force is nearby.

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:47.390
Find them and destroy them.

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:56.730
Look! It's the 4th Platoon!

00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:49.030
The 3rd and 5th Platoons...

00:16:49.030 --> 00:16:50.930
And Willant's Gunbus!

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:55.500
What? From the southern gate?

00:16:55.500 --> 00:16:56.940
Report!

00:16:56.940 --> 00:17:00.290
Arandas Trail Kriegers have entered the base!

00:17:18.060 --> 00:17:19.910
This is a problem.

00:17:20.900 --> 00:17:21.760
Major!

00:17:26.240 --> 00:17:28.110
The demon of Arandas!

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:44.380
Stop, Major!

00:17:44.380 --> 00:17:46.880
I can't let the soldiers die for nothing.

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:48.840
But with just one machine...

00:17:48.840 --> 00:17:51.330
If nothing else, I can buy time.

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:52.480
Then I'll go, too...

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:55.510
You command the retreat.

00:17:55.510 --> 00:17:57.640
Get as many of the men back alive as you can.

00:17:57.640 --> 00:17:58.890
That's an order.

00:17:59.400 --> 00:18:00.900
I'm counting on you.

00:18:35.430 --> 00:18:37.640
So this is the demon of Arandas?

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:41.560
I see... It's not like any Trail Krieger I've ever seen.

00:19:03.420 --> 00:19:04.420
Major!

00:19:06.420 --> 00:19:07.420
He's out of bullets?

00:19:16.890 --> 00:19:17.640
Major!

00:19:17.640 --> 00:19:18.640
I'm not dead yet!

00:19:57.590 --> 00:19:58.830
What is this?

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:11.940
Always save your best card for last.

00:20:47.910 --> 00:20:49.270
Command to all units.

00:20:49.270 --> 00:20:51.090
Mission complete.

00:20:51.090 --> 00:20:53.530
Repeat. Mission complete.

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:25.290
Two glasses.

00:23:36.560 --> 00:23:39.480
End of Absence
